    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0350" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg276"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Hale.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 4, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Secretary of the Navy has instructed
                    Admiral Goldsborough to send a proper national armed vessel to Alexandria to
                    receive from you John H. Surratt, a citizen of the United States, who is in your
                    custody as an arrested fugitive, charged with the crime of assassination of the
                    late Abraham Lincoln, President of the United States, and of an attempt to
                    assassinate William H. Seward, Secretary of State of the United States, in the
                    month of April, 1865. You will deliver the before-named to the commanding
                    officer of the vessel upon his reporting to you his arrival at Alexandria.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Hale,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
